[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2709090255","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98491#issuecomment-2709090255","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98491","id":2709090255,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6heW_P","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T22:00:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T22:00:35Z","body":"I think I stumbled to the same bug. I have a UI where player presses a button to assign bonus points to player's attributes and I'm using the `button_down` signal instead of `pressed` signal (that's a design choice). When there are no more points to assign, the button is disabled. After a while the button is enabled again. Now the bug happens, button doesn't send `button_down` signal with the first click. I need to click the button twice to get a `button_down` signal. It seems that the previous `button_up` was totally ignored because the button was already disabled. And without `button_up` signal, `button_down` signal cannot happen.\n\nI haven't looked the C++ code at all, but resetting the button's i